what's going on everybody it's warren  welcome back to the cosmic wonder where  we talk all things marvel and mcu  spiderman no way home has been in  theaters for over a month now coming up  on two months and the writers and the  production team and the actors they're  all doing tours right now and they're  all doing interviews and of course as  they do interviews and get asked  questions more about the film comes out  including what we actually missed scenes  that almost made it to the final cut but  were cut out right before they decided  on what the finale was and for those  mysterio fans we almost got mysterio in  the final battle for spider-man no way  home and not just mysterio but some  other villains as well and sadly we do  actually have a little bit of a tease of  what this could have looked like as well  as marvel has released official concept  art of this final scene and mysterio in  it fighting doctor strange the writers  have shed some light on what the scene  actually was and how mysterio and rhino  came into the final battle of spider-man  home so let's break down what they said  and of course if you're new and you love  marvel be sure to subscribe and hit the  notification bell so you don't miss out  on any of the latest videos so in an  interview with comicbook.com spider-man  no way home writers chris mckenna and  eric sommers talk about how we almost  actually did have a sinister six and in  this interview they explained that they  kept going over who should the sixth  villain be who was going to be the final  member of the sinister six and before  they decided to not have a sixth member  the two options that they had on the  table were going to be either mysterio  or rhino and i personally would have  loved to see mysterio show up in  spiderman no way home because it would  have been a different mysterio it  wouldn't have been the same quentin back  that we saw in spider-man far from home  and this would have added a bit of a  twist to everything because in that  final battle people probably would have  seen mysterio which would have added  some confusion considering the fact that  he's dead in the mcu or should i say the  main timeline but perhaps the biggest  thing that we were robbed of because  this did not make the final cut was a  fight between mysterio and dr strange as  i mentioned official concept art for  spider-man no way home has come out and  it shows mysterio fighting doctor  strange at the statue of liberty now  this would have been a very interesting  battle because doctor strange is magic  but mysterio is not he's an illusionist  he's the master of illusions so it would  have been interesting to see how he held  up against doctor strange using his  illusions would this have been confusing  to doctor strange or would it have  simply been just a walk in the park for  doctor strange true magic versus  illusions despite whatever it may have  been i'm sure it would have looked  phenomenal now instead of getting  mysterio or rhino as the sixth member of  the sinister six they kind of came  through at the end where the multiverse  starts to kind of tear apart and all of  the villains who know that peter parker  spider-man are coming through in a real  quick blink and you'll miss it moments  we can see people like craven the hunter  and of course mysterio and rhino are  there as well so ultimately that is what  they decided on instead of having that  one last member of the sinister six  however the writers do go on to say that  they really thought about doing the  official sinister six in this movie  chris mckenna says who is the sinister  six here if you want six you can always  say venom was the sixth member if you  want he's in the tag he made it into the  mcu but he never made it out of mexico  there was always that talk of should we  be doing officially the six now  ultimately they didn't but here's  something that is truly interesting the  writers also revealed that the green  goblin was originally not the main  villain of the film but they lost  characters and as they lost certain  characters the green goblin became the  main villain of the film so you have to  wonder who they lost and if they lost  them because sony and marvel are  actually planning on using them for an  official sinister six movie sony  executive producer amy pascal once said  about two years ago that if you look at  everybody in the mcu we actually have  all of the members of the sinister six  already so perhaps that's why we didn't  get an official sinister six in this  movie because sony and marvel have other  plans for the sinister six and of course  a new spider-man trilogy has been  announced with tom holland perhaps  they're waiting for him right around the  corner in another movie but i would have  really liked to see mysterio in that  final battle go up against doctor  strange and the spider-man but let me  know what you think about this in the  comments down below would you have liked  to have seen rhino show up or mysterio  or perhaps maybe even both a sinister  seven let me know your thoughts and  don't forget to like the video and  subscribe so you don't miss out on any  of the latest news for live updates you  can follow me on instagram and twitter  and as always thank you all so much for  watching woof  you
 

